      "mergeID": "691c9c9aad5008b9c8b40154",
      "mergedPostDetails": "When viewing avatar details of a public avatar from a local client, randomly, the Acknowledgements section is unavailable. This occurs with both pressing the \"View Avatar Details\" button and also when switching between \"My Avatars\" and \"My Current Avatar\" tabs.\n\nThis also occurs randomly for remote users viewing my currently displayed public avatar via the new Avatar Details page accessed via my profile. I don't think it's API rate limiting related, but random (maybe a network latency or code race condition).\n\nThis is a bug, because often avatar creators need to include and display acknowledgements / attribution for license compliance.\n\nExample public avatars with acknowledgements sections for testing:\n\n- Fsh the Fish (avtr_f5b56d2a-8046-4c65-a943-301abbb0594f) by Duskstar Shine\n\n- Skylar (avtr_4768f0aa-2879-484f-b8f2-e818d53a3f44) by Pylon?",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Acknowledgements section in avatar details of public avatars are not viewable randomly",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "69147e707699bc1f058043da",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
