  "details": "When a remote user in VRChat client navigates to my profile and presses View Avatar Details while I am wearing a private avatar, they cannot see the Acknowledgements section on that avatar. However, I can see them locally in \"My Current Avatar\", \"My Avatars\" avatar details, and on the website. This also happens in reverse, where I cannot see my friend's private avatar's Acknowledgements section.\n\nThis seems to only affect private avatars. The acknowledgements section of public avatars can be viewed (albeit [Acknowledgements section in avatar details of public avatars are not viewable randomly](https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/acknowledgements-section-in-avatar-details-of-public-avatars-are-not-viewable-ra)).\n\nThis is a bug, because often avatar creators need to include and display acknowledgements / attribution for license compliance while in the same world instance.\n\nA sample avatar IDs uploaded by me, with acknowledgements sections (private): `avtr_8a33bffc-c9dd-45a5-a18e-55a18a31c0ef`.\n\nThe screenshots attached show what a remote user sees about my avatar and what I see about my avatar in the avatar details.",
